Re: Cheyenne Public Safety Center Additional Services Request
Dear Mark,
Items affecting design and construction for this project have developed which are either
beyond the originally contracted scope of work, or the time frame originally developed by the
contractor.
Below are outlined the specific tasks and costs associated with each item. We
respectfully ask for the City’s approval of this request for additional services for your new
facility.
The total sum for the additional architectural and engineering services will be $101,323.00.
The additional services are as follows:
1. Scope of the Program
Increasing the building GSF from 86,685 SF to 93,919 SF. Program area designed increased
from 63,000 SFto 67,179 SF. Value added to project = 4,176 SF x $100/SF @7% design
fee = $29,253.
2. Change in Structural Engineering and Architectural Needs
The added mechanical penthouse required additional structural engineering and
architectural coordination. Additionally, field investigation discovered that the east building
required lateral bracing enhancements to offset alterations and removal of a prior interior
structural wall (MMW FEE: $21,500— see attachment; J. Senger: 16 hours @ $1 75/hr =
$2,800). The total sum for the additional structural engineering and architectural needs is
$24,300. See attached letter.
3. Additional Foundation Options
Coordination meetings and communication with Hayward Baker, FCI Contractors, Lt.
Munari, Martin / Martin, and lnberg Miller to discuss additional foundation options because
of unforeseen conditions with the bearing capacity of the soil in the 1960s building over a
three month period U. Senger: 16 hours @ $1 75/hr). The total sum for the additional
foundation options is $2,800.
4. Antenna Tower Installation
Time to help specify the LCEMA Tower, coordination meetings and communication with
Motorola, Lt. Munari, Glen Crumpton, Rohn, and LCEMA between. Also designing antenna
guardrail on penthouse, and locating towers on roof white understanding interferences ci.
Senger: 24 hours @ $175/hr). The total sum to see the antenna tower installation through is
$4,200.
