June 1, 2016
Lt. Mark Munari
Cheyenne Police Department
415 West 18” Street
Cheyenne, WY 82001
Re: Cheyenne Public Safety Center Additional Services Request
Dear Mark,
I would like to thank you and Chief Kozak for meeting with me and Ed Bledowski of the DLR Group
this morning to discuss the items in our add services request, date January 26, 2016. Our discussion
focused on two items that were of concern; item #1, which addressed a scope change to the project,
and item #5, which address a contract extension.
Item #1 requested additional fee for changes due to the increased scope of the project. The explanation
dealt with an increase in square footage, which our contract does not address. Our contract does,
however, identify a construction budget of $1 8.2M, but the current cost is presently just over $20.4M,
a growth in scope of over 10%.
Item #5 requested additional fee for the extension of the project duration.
It is asking additional
construction administration fees for DLR Group to cover a three-month extension period. In reality, the
project has extended 5 months.
During our discussion, it was agreed by all that the project has been extended by five months and that
additional fee was warranted.
Even though it has been extended by five months, DLR Group is still
only requesting the amount submitted for the three-month extension.
Regarding the increase in fee due to increased scope identified in item #1, it was agreed that the scope
did increase, however, the city had issues with some problems that they felt were design related, and
that the architect bore some responsibility for.
DLR Group agreed to drop the request for the scope fee
increase as remuneration for design related problems. Everyone was very comfortable with this
compromise.
To recap, item #1, in the amount of $29,253, will be dropped from the add services request, leaving
items 2 through 7 as valid items for payment.
Please note that Pappas & Pappas Architects has not
applied a mark-up on any of the additional fees requested by our consultants.
Please let me know if this accurately expresses the discussion and decisions reached in our meeting this
morning. Thanks so much for taking the time to meet with us.
Sincerely,
Stephan A. Pappas, AlA, LEED AP
C:
Chief Brian Kozak
Ed Bledowski
A
EXHIBIT
‘5,
